Z||000003||007DOUG||08-30-2000||10:16 PM||||I'll never take another 4 cyl. out the bottom again. See link:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierowarehouse/topswap.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierowarehouse/topswap.html</A> <P>I doubt this will work on V6's.<P>------------------<BR>4 Indy pace Cars<BR>84 T-top<BR>84 SE<BR>86 SE V6 153K<BR>2 86 GT's<BR>86 GT 3.4 Pearl White T-top<BR>2 88 GT twins<P>However......<BR><I>"Time is my most precious and most perishable of all my possessions."</I>||||reg||6
Z||000004||ThatRickGuy||08-31-2000||12:07 AM||||you can with a V-6, but it's easier to go out the bottom. out the top you have to strip a lot off. it's so much easier to push it onto a hoist, pull the harness, a few cables, and bolts, lift the car, and watch the craddle lay there. with the 4 tho, it'll probrably be easier... expecially the reinstall.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Brian84SE||08-31-2000||05:51 AM||||Thanks guys,<BR>Guess what I'll be doing this labor day weekend?||||reg||1
Z||000006||BN Boomer||08-31-2000||12:50 PM||||Hey, what's this, a V-6 going back in from the top? Well whaddaya know!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/boomers_fiero_files/fiero1.jpg"> <P>Actually, I think it's <I>easier</I> to pull/reinstall a V-6 from the top than the 4 cyl. And you don't have to strip off as many, if any more, parts or accessories than you would with the 4 cyl. Plus, the V-6 is shorter overall than the 4 cyl, making it easier to seperate from the tranny and lift out. ||||reg||14
